al position, 0-100 percent.","deviceId":"divert2","direction":"world_to_plc","id":"D2_Position","name":"D2_Position","normalValue":0,"role":"divert2.position"},{"dataType":"UDINT","description":"Encoder counts from belt travel, quantised, UDINT wrap; PLC owns scaling.","deviceId":"drive","direction":"world_to_plc","id":"Encoder_Count","name":"Encoder_Count","normalValue":0,"role":"motion.encoderCount"},{"dataType":"BOOL","description":"PLC command to the belt drive. Cartons move only if the simulated drive actually runs.","deviceId":"drive","direction":"plc_to_world","id":"Motor_RunCmd","name":"Motor_RunCmd","normalValue":false,"role":"drive.runCommand"},{"dataType":"BOOL","description":"Extend divert 1 to exit A; deassert returns home.","deviceId":"divert1","direction":"plc_to_world","id":"D1_ExtendCmd","name":"D1_ExtendCmd","normalValue":false,"role":"divert1.extendCommand"},{"dataType":"BOOL","description":"Extend divert 2 to exit B; deassert returns home.","deviceId":"divert2","direction":"plc_to_world","id":"D2_ExtendCmd","name":"D2_ExtendCmd","normalValue":false,"role":"divert2.extendCommand"},{"dataType":"BOOL","description":"Optional visible machine-fault indication.","deviceId":"stacklight","direction":"plc_to_world","id":"StackLight_Red","name":"StackLight_Red","normalValue":false,"role":"indication.stackRed"},{"dataType":"BOOL","description":"Optional visible running/ready indication.","deviceId":"stacklight","direction":"plc_to_world","id":"StackLight_Green","name":"StackLight_Green","normalValue":false,"role":"indication.stackGreen"}],"stateSchemaVersion":"1.0.0","tickMs":100,"worldId":"m8-conveyor-1.0.2"},"physicalParameters":[{"basis":"specified","name":"beltNominalSpeedMps","source":"spec §2 variant parameter","unit":"m/s","value":"0.30"},{"basis":"specified","name":"cartonLengthM","source":"spec §2 suggested starting value","unit":"m","value":"0.30"},{"basis":"specified","name":"divertTravelTimeS","source":"spec §2 suggested starting value (each divert)","unit":"s","value":"0.35"},{"basis":"inferred","name":"driveAccelMps2","source":"inferred — no accel given in spec","unit":"m/s^2","value":"0.60"},{"basis":"inferred","name":"driveDecelMps2","source":"inferred — coast dynamics required by §3.4 but unquantified","unit":"m/s^2","value":"0.60"},{"basis":"inferred","name":"encoderCountsPerMeter","source":"inferred — encoder density not specified; PLC owns scaling","unit":"counts/m","value":"1000"},{"basis":"inferred","name":"driveFeedbackDelayS","source":"inferred — §4 requires delayed feedback, no value","unit":"s","value":"0.10"},{"basis":"inferred","name":"divertDecisionThresholdPct","source":"inferred — carton follows actual position (§1), threshold unspecified","unit":"%","value":"80"},{"basis":"inferred","name":"sensorPositionsM","source":"inferred geometry — spec gives order only (§2 diagram)","unit":"m","value":"Entry 0.30, D1Approach 1.00, D1 decision 1.40, D2Approach 2.00, D2 decision 2.40, ExitA 2.00 (A branch), ExitB 3.00 (B branch), Runout 3.20"}],"questions":[{"blocking":false,"id":"Q-01","question":"Should fault.setDriveFeedbackFailure mean the drive physically does not run (current model, giving R-11's 'no virtual motion'), or that the motor runs but only its feedback is lost (cartons would move while PLC sees no feedback)? The spec supports both readings (§4 vs §8/R-11).","relatesTo":"R-11"},{"blocking":false,"id":"Q-02","question":"No sensor positions, spacing distances, acceleration/deceleration rates, encoder counts-per-metre, drive-feedback delay, or divert decision threshold are specified. The world uses labelled inferred values; confirm none of them will be scored as acceptance thresholds.","relatesTo":"R-01..R-04"},{"blocking":false,"id":"Q-03","question":"Detection deadlines/thresholds for drive-start fault (R-11), divert failure (R-13/R-14), jam timeout (R-19), debounce (R-09) and stuck-sensor plausibility (R-10) are all TBD in §9; checks are marked unspecified-basis until the engineer freezes them.","relatesTo":"R-09..R-19"},{"blocking":false,"id":"Q-04","question":"Blocked-destination and runout-blocked policies (§11.2) are accepted demo defaults but §9 marks R-06/R-07 PROBE; confirm whether they may be scored as MUST for the campaign.","relatesTo":"R-06,R-07"},{"blocking":false,"id":"Q-05","question":"WCS offer/ack/completion, operator Start/Stop/Reset, mode and counts are supervisory symbols outside the 25-signal bench map (§4/§5). Which connector symbols will the campaign use to drive and observe them, and what are the State_Code/Fault_Code enumerations?","relatesTo":"R-02..R-08,R-20"},{"blocking":false,"id":"Q-06","question":"Exact BenchSimulationActive selection action, Bench_HostHeartbeat type/timeout and stale-value behaviour on disconnect (§4/§7) are TBD; startup/transport checks cannot be scored until frozen.","relatesTo":"R-21"},{"blocking":false,"id":"Q-07","question":"Should the overload fault physically trip/stop the belt (current model) or only assert the Drive_Overload input while the drive keeps running until the PLC reacts?","relatesTo":"R-12"}],"summary":"Executable external-physics world for the slow-belt (0.30 m/s) M8 conveyor on map m8-conveyor-1.0.2: continuous belt drive with accel/coast-decel, geometric photoeyes derived from carton position/length, two 0.35 s two-position diverts whose actual position decides each carton's branch at the decision point, quantised wrapping UDINT encoder from belt travel, downstream readiness, and the declared fault knobs (drive feedback failure, overload trip, divert jam, contradictory limits, stuck/bouncing sensors, carton jam). The world implements no PLC sequencing, routing, counting or alarm logic. world.test.ts checks physical invariants (no motion without drive, deceleration on stop, encoder proportional to travel, sensors from position, divert travel/feedback, diverted carton reaches only its exit). The test plan covers R-01…R-23 plus I/O/startup checks, marking PROBE/TBD expectations as unspecified-basis rather than inventing thresholds. No PLC test was run during preparation.","testPlan":{"checks":[{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"With no carton and no commands, the complete input image is written every cycle: all photoeyes false, D1/D2 home true and extended false, Drive_RunningFB false, Drive_Overload false, ExitA/ExitB/Runout ready true, Belt_SpeedActual 0, D1/D2_Position 0, Encoder_Count constant.","group":"io","id":"IO-01","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Normal simulated DI state with no carton matches §4.","observeSignals":["PE_Entry","PE_D1Approach","PE_D2Approach","PE_ExitA","PE_ExitB","PE_Runout","D1_HomeFB","D1_ExtendedFB","D2_HomeFB","D2_ExtendedFB","Drive_RunningFB","Drive_Overload","ExitA_Ready","ExitB_Ready","Runout_Ready","Belt_SpeedActual","Drive_Current","D1_Position","D2_Position","Encoder_Count"],"requirementRefs":["DI-01..DI-15","DO-01..DO-05"],"sourceRefs":["§4 I/O table and normal-state paragraph"],"stimulus":"Initialise the bench world (no carton.introduce, no PLC outputs, no faults) and observe several 10 Hz input frames.","title":"Normal no-carton input image at 10 Hz","worldControls":[]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"Bench setup fails visibly on any missing, mistyped or stale required tag rather than substituting values; in the passing case all 25 bench signals are present with the declared types.","group":"io","id":"IO-02","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Connector validates the exact signal map instead of quietly substituting values.","observeSignals":["PE_Entry","Drive_RunningFB","Encoder_Count","Motor_RunCmd","D1_ExtendCmd","D2_ExtendCmd"],"requirementRefs":[],"sourceRefs":["§4 final I/O map paragraph","§7","§10"],"stimulus":"Run connector map discovery against map m8-conveyor-1.0.2 and compare id/direction/type of every signal with the manifest.","title":"Signal map completeness and typing","worldControls":[]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED: the spec requires a deliberate action to select simulated inputs and BenchSimulationActive to confirm it (§3.1, §4), but the exact selection UI/block grouping and timeout are implementation details/TBD, so no scored threshold is stated.","group":"startup","id":"ST-01","needsHmi":true,"objective":"Startup defaults to physical I/O passthrough; simulated inputs require a deliberate selection confirmed by BenchSimulationActive.","observeSignals":["Motor_RunCmd","PE_Entry","Drive_RunningFB"],"requirementRefs":[],"sourceRefs":["§3 items 1","§4 application status table","§11"],"stimulus":"Power up / restart the PLC without selecting bench mode, observe that world inputs do not drive the application; then perform the deliberate bench-mode selection action and observe BenchSimulationActive (supervisory symbol, outside the 25-signal map).","title":"Startup passthrough then deliberate bench-mode selection","worldControls":[]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"Stop removes Motor_RunCmd and inhibits new feed; the carton decelerates per drive dynamics then remains fixed; Belt_SpeedActual falls to 0, Drive_RunningFB and Encoder_Count stay consistent with the coast (encoder stops when the belt stops); the line is not drained.","group":"normal","id":"R-01","needsHmi":true,"objective":"Stop removes the run command, inhibits feed, cartons coast to rest and stay; no drain-to-empty.","observeSignals":["Motor_RunCmd","Drive_RunningFB","Belt_SpeedActual","Encoder_Count","PE_Entry","PE_D1Approach"],"requirementRefs":["R-01"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-01","§3 item 4"],"stimulus":"Start via operator command, introduce one carton, let it travel mid-lane, then issue operator Stop; observe outputs and inputs over the stopping interval and after settling.","title":"Start/stop and no motion after stopping settles","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"D1_ExtendCmd actuates early enough that D1_ExtendedFB is reached before the carton decision point; exactly one PE_ExitA passage and one A completion/count; no PE_ExitB or PE_Runout passage for that carton.","group":"normal","id":"R-02","needsHmi":false,"objective":"A-assigned carton is diverted at D1 to exit A exactly once.","observeSignals":["D1_ExtendCmd","D1_ExtendedFB","D1_HomeFB","D1_Position","PE_D1Approach","PE_ExitA","PE_ExitB","PE_Runout","Motor_RunCmd"],"requirementRefs":["R-02"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-02","§2 nominal cycle","§3 item 3"],"stimulus":"WCS offers a carton with route A (supervisory), PLC releases, world introduces one carton while the belt runs.","title":"Normal A sort","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"Carton passes D1 (PE_D1Approach, then PE_D2Approach), D2_ExtendCmd actuates in time with D2_ExtendedFB before the D2 decision point; exactly one PE_ExitB passage and one B completion/count; no runout passage.","group":"normal","id":"R-03","needsHmi":false,"objective":"B-assigned carton passes D1 and is diverted at D2 to exit B exactly once.","observeSignals":["D2_ExtendCmd","D2_ExtendedFB","D2_HomeFB","D2_Position","PE_D1Approach","PE_D2Approach","PE_ExitB","PE_Runout"],"requirementRefs":["R-03"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-03","§3 item 3"],"stimulus":"WCS offers route B, PLC releases, introduce one carton.","title":"Normal B sort","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"Carton continues straight: PE_D1Approach and PE_D2Approach then exactly one PE_Runout passage; disposition reported runout-unassigned; no machine fault and no A/B sort count.","group":"normal","id":"R-04","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Unassigned carton runs out straight as a normal disposition.","observeSignals":["PE_Entry","PE_D1Approach","PE_D2Approach","PE_Runout","PE_ExitA","PE_ExitB","Motor_RunCmd"],"requirementRefs":["R-04"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-04","§1","§11"],"stimulus":"No WCS route (or route Unknown); PLC releases on runout availability; introduce one carton.","title":"Normal runout (jackpot) for unassigned carton","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED as a scored oracle (PROBE): §3.3/§5 require only that a late route must not retroactively count as a successful A sort and the actual disposition be reported; the exact late-B policy and reporting wording are TBD.","group":"functional","id":"R-05","needsHmi":false,"objective":"A route arriving after its decision point is not claimed as a successful sort.","observeSignals":["D1_ExtendCmd","D1_ExtendedFB","PE_D1Approach","PE_Runout","PE_ExitA"],"requirementRefs":["R-05"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-05 (PROBE)","§3 item 3","§5"],"stimulus":"Introduce a carton with no route; after it passes the D1 decision point, deliver a WCS offer assigning A; observe divert commands, exit passage and reported disposition.","title":"Late route after D1 decision point","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED as scored behaviour (PROBE with an accepted demo default in §11.2: send to runout with an exception, never count the blocked exit as successful). Confirm the policy before scoring.","group":"functional","id":"R-06","needsHmi":false,"objective":"A carton assigned to a blocked destination is never counted as a successful sort at that exit.","observeSignals":["ExitA_Ready","D1_ExtendCmd","PE_ExitA","PE_Runout","Motor_RunCmd"],"requirementRefs":["R-06"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-06 (PROBE)","§11 default 2","§5 downstream"],"stimulus":"Set ExitA not ready before an A-assigned carton reaches D1; introduce the carton and observe routing and reported disposition.","title":"Destination A not ready before decision point","worldControls":["downstream.setReady","carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED (PROBE): proposed feed inhibit and belt stop before congestion (§11.2) is a demo policy to confirm before scoring; observe and record the actual PLC response.","group":"functional","id":"R-07","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Runout blocked with an unroutable carton approaching.","observeSignals":["Runout_Ready","Motor_RunCmd","PE_Runout","PE_D2Approach"],"requirementRefs":["R-07"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-07 (PROBE)","§3 item 3","§11 default 2"],"stimulus":"Set Runout_Ready false, introduce an unassigned carton and observe feed/belt behaviour as it approaches runout.","title":"Runout blocked","worldControls":["downstream.setReady","carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"The duplicate offer creates no second carton, no second completion and no extra count (observed via PLC supervisory counts/completion and exactly one physical carton passage).","group":"functional","id":"R-08","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Duplicate WCS sequence/item does not create a second carton or completion.","observeSignals":["PE_Entry","PE_ExitA","PE_ExitB","PE_Runout"],"requirementRefs":["R-08"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-08","§5 OfferAck"],"stimulus":"Send the same CartonOffer (same sequence and item ID) twice through the WCS emulator; introduce at most the single released carton.","title":"Duplicate WCS offer","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED (PROBE): no duplicate item/count or unstable divert decision is the proposed oracle, but the debounce threshold and injection method are TBD (§9) and sub-100 ms bounce may not traverse the transport (§7). Record PLC behaviour without scoring a threshold.","group":"faults","id":"R-09","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Entry/approach photoeye bounce causes no duplicate item/count or unstable divert decision.","observeSignals":["PE_Entry","PE_D1Approach","D1_ExtendCmd","PE_ExitA","PE_Runout"],"requirementRefs":["R-09"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-09 (PROBE)","§7 timing gate","§8 fault knobs"],"stimulus":"Enable sensor bounce on PE_Entry (then PE_D1Approach) while introducing and running one carton.","title":"Sensor bounce on entry / approach photoeye","worldControls":["fault.setSensorBounce","carton.introduce","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED (PROBE): timeout/plausibility evidence with no invented completion is proposed; the PLC reaction threshold is TBD. Record whether the PLC flags the implausibility and what it reports.","group":"faults","id":"R-10","needsHmi":false,"objective":"A photoeye stuck true or false against carton movement produces no invented completion.","observeSignals":["PE_Entry","PE_D1Approach","PE_ExitA","PE_Runout","Motor_RunCmd"],"requirementRefs":["R-10"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-10 (PROBE)","§8 fault knobs"],"stimulus":"Stick PE_Entry true (in a second run, stick PE_D1Approach false) while a carton travels the lane.","title":"Stuck photoeye","worldControls":["fault.setSensorStuck","carton.introduce","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"PLC detects a drive-start fault (fault indication via supervisory state/stack light), the carton does not move (photoeyes/encoder confirm no travel) and no completion is reported. Detection deadline is TBD, so timing is recorded, not scored.","group":"faults","id":"R-11","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Motor commanded without running feedback is detected as a drive-start fault with no virtual motion or false completion.","observeSignals":["Motor_RunCmd","Drive_RunningFB","Belt_SpeedActual","Encoder_Count","PE_Entry","StackLight_Red"],"requirementRefs":["R-11"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-11","§4 DI-11","§8"],"stimulus":"Enable drive feedback failure, Start the PLC so Motor_RunCmd asserts, and introduce a carton.","title":"Motor command without feedback","worldControls":["fault.setDriveFeedbackFailure","carton.introduce","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"PLC removes Motor_RunCmd, stops new feed, shows the fault (supervisory fault state / StackLight_Red); after clearing the fault and issuing Reset the belt does not auto-restart until a new Start.","group":"faults","id":"R-12","needsHmi":true,"objective":"Overload during travel removes the motor command, stops feed, faults, and does not auto-restart after reset.","observeSignals":["Drive_Overload","Motor_RunCmd","Drive_RunningFB","Belt_SpeedActual","StackLight_Red","PE_Entry"],"requirementRefs":["R-12"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-12","§3 items 4-5"],"stimulus":"Run a carton mid-lane, assert the overload fault; then clear it and issue operator Reset, observing for any automatic restart.","title":"Motor overload / trip during travel","worldControls":["fault.setOverload","carton.introduce","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"The carton follows the actual (home) divert position to runout; the PLC reports a misroute, not an A completion/count; any fault indication and its deadline are recorded (deadline TBD).","group":"faults","id":"R-13","needsHmi":false,"objective":"D1 failing to move on an A assignment results in misroute reporting, never an A completion.","observeSignals":["D1_ExtendCmd","D1_HomeFB","D1_ExtendedFB","D1_Position","PE_ExitA","PE_Runout"],"requirementRefs":["R-13"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-13","§1 (actual position governs)","§11 default 1"],"stimulus":"Jam divert 1, assign route A, introduce one carton and run it to its exit.","title":"D1 fails to move on A assignment","worldControls":["fault.setDivertJam","carton.introduce","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"Carton reaches runout and is reported misrouted, not a B completion/count; fault indication/deadline recorded (deadline TBD).","group":"faults","id":"R-14","needsHmi":false,"objective":"D2 failing to move on a B assignment results in misroute reporting, never a B completion.","observeSignals":["D2_ExtendCmd","D2_HomeFB","D2_ExtendedFB","D2_Position","PE_ExitB","PE_Runout"],"requirementRefs":["R-14"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-14","§1","§11 default 1"],"stimulus":"Jam divert 2, assign route B, introduce one carton and run it through.","title":"D2 fails to move on B assignment","worldControls":["fault.setDivertJam","carton.introduce","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED (PROBE): the PLC must not claim a verified divert from contradictory feedback; exact alarm behaviour is TBD. Record fault/indication response.","group":"faults","id":"R-15","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Simultaneous home+extended feedback is exposed as inconsistent and not treated as a verified divert.","observeSignals":["D1_HomeFB","D1_ExtendedFB","D1_Position","D1_ExtendCmd","PE_ExitA","PE_Runout"],"requirementRefs":["R-15"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-15 (PROBE)","§4 DI-07..DI-10"],"stimulus":"Enable contradictory limits on D1 during an A-assigned run (repeat for D2 in a second run).","title":"Contradictory divert limits","worldControls":["fault.setContradictoryLimits","carton.introduce","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED (PROBE): no double completion/count and a reported contradiction are proposed; no generic alarm behaviour is assumed. The world cannot produce this physically with one carton, so it is injected only as stuck-sensor combinations and labelled as an injected input fault, not physical truth.","group":"faults","id":"R-16","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Simultaneous exit photoeyes for one carton produce no double completion/count.","observeSignals":["PE_ExitA","PE_ExitB","PE_Runout","PE_Entry"],"requirementRefs":["R-16"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-16 (PROBE)","§9 exploration note"],"stimulus":"With one carton on the lane, stick a second exit photoeye true so two exit beams read simultaneously; observe PLC completion/count behaviour.","title":"Impossible exit combination with one carton","worldControls":["fault.setSensorStuck","carton.introduce","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED (PROBE): identify the suspect sequence and avoid an unearned pass; do not assume one generic PLC alarm is required (§9 R-17).","group":"faults","id":"R-17","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Out-of-order sensor sequence is not credited as a valid sort.","observeSignals":["PE_Entry","PE_D2Approach","PE_ExitB","PE_Runout"],"requirementRefs":["R-17"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-17 (PROBE)"],"stimulus":"Stick PE_D2Approach true before any entry event for a carton (injected sequence fault), then run one carton and observe PLC item/completion handling.","title":"Impossible sensor sequence","worldControls":["fault.setSensorStuck","carton.introduce","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED (PROBE): record the diagnostic response; whether it reveals an unsafe or incorrectly counted state is a review decision (§9 R-18), not a scored oracle.","group":"faults","id":"R-18","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Command/feedback disagreement is recorded and diagnosed.","observeSignals":["Motor_RunCmd","Drive_RunningFB","D1_ExtendCmd","D1_ExtendedFB","Belt_SpeedActual"],"requirementRefs":["R-18"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-18 (PROBE)"],"stimulus":"With Motor_RunCmd off, stick Drive_RunningFB true via the feedback path (or hold D1 extended feedback while its command is off using sensor-stuck on D1_ExtendedFB) and observe the PLC response.","title":"Command/feedback disagreement","worldControls":["fault.setSensorStuck","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"PLC produces a timeout/fault or equivalent and no invented completion for the jammed carton. The timeout threshold is TBD, so elapsed time is recorded, not scored.","group":"faults","id":"R-19","needsHmi":false,"objective":"A carton held at a divert/runout while the drive runs yields a jam response and no invented completion.","observeSignals":["Motor_RunCmd","Drive_RunningFB","Belt_SpeedActual","Encoder_Count","PE_D1Approach","PE_Runout","StackLight_Red"],"requirementRefs":["R-19"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-19","§8 fault knobs"],"stimulus":"Run a carton onto the lane, enable the carton jam so it holds position while the belt continues to run; observe PLC response over time.","title":"Carton jam while drive runs","worldControls":["fault.setCartonJam","carton.introduce","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED (PROBE): visible link state and runout/hold per policy with no duplicate completion on retry are proposed; the governing policy is undecided (§9 R-20, §5).","group":"edge","id":"R-20","needsHmi":false,"objective":"WCS link loss and recovery are visible and cause no duplicate completion.","observeSignals":["PE_Entry","PE_Runout","Motor_RunCmd"],"requirementRefs":["R-20"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-20 (PROBE)","§5"],"stimulus":"Pause WCS messages/heartbeat mid-run (WCS emulator action, outside the field-I/O map), then resume and retry; observe link state and completions.","title":"WCS link loss and recovery","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"Stale evidence is labelled as such, no test is passed on stale data, the disconnect is recorded, and the affected test is inconclusive if the controller cannot be observed (§7).","group":"runtime","id":"R-21","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Transport interruption yields labelled stale evidence and no false pass.","observeSignals":["Motor_RunCmd","Drive_RunningFB","PE_Entry","Belt_SpeedActual"],"requirementRefs":["R-21"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-21","§7 disconnect paragraph"],"stimulus":"Break and reconnect the workstation transport during a run; examine evidence timestamps/quality and the recorded verdict handling.","title":"Transport (OPC UA) interruption during a run","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"Each HMI button action produces a visible acknowledgement/resulting state that agrees with the actual PLC mode/output state; Reset acknowledges without erasing the fault cause or auto-restarting (UI-01..UI-04).","group":"runtime","id":"R-22","needsHmi":true,"objective":"HMI Start/Stop/Reset/Auto actions, displayed state and actual PLC state agree.","observeSignals":["Motor_RunCmd","Drive_RunningFB","D1_ExtendCmd","D1_ExtendedFB","StackLight_Red","StackLight_Green"],"requirementRefs":["R-22","UI-01","UI-02","UI-03","UI-04"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-22","§6 UI table"],"stimulus":"Operate Start, Stop, Reset and Auto solely through the visible PLC HMI (WebVisu) with timestamped screenshot evidence, cross-checked against signal traces.","title":"HMI congruence via visible controls","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"unspecified","expectedObservation":"UNSPECIFIED (PROBE/stretch): each carton reaches one correct exit without identity merge or conflicting divert timing is the proposed oracle; multi-carton spacing is deferred/exploratory (§2, §11.5).","group":"edge","id":"R-23","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Two close cartons with different routes each reach one correct exit without identity merge.","observeSignals":["PE_Entry","PE_D1Approach","PE_D2Approach","D1_ExtendCmd","D2_ExtendCmd","PE_ExitA","PE_ExitB","PE_Runout"],"requirementRefs":["R-23"],"sourceRefs":["§9 R-23 (PROBE/stretch)","§2"],"stimulus":"Introduce two cartons in flight (first assigned B, second assigned A) with the belt running; observe divert timing and each exit passage.","title":"Multi-carton spacing (stretch)","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"Reset acknowledges the cleared fault (fault indication clears) and the belt does not restart until a new Start command; WCS/HMI show the resulting state.","group":"functional","id":"FN-01","needsHmi":true,"objective":"Reset acknowledges a cleared fault without automatically restarting the belt.","observeSignals":["Drive_Overload","Motor_RunCmd","Drive_RunningFB","StackLight_Red","Belt_SpeedActual"],"requirementRefs":[],"sourceRefs":["§3 item 5","§6 (acknowledge controls)"],"stimulus":"Raise and clear an overload fault, issue operator Reset, wait, then issue Start and observe the two distinct transitions.","title":"Reset does not auto-restart","worldControls":["fault.setOverload","fault.clearAll"]},{"expectedBasis":"specified","expectedObservation":"While Motor_RunCmd is false and the drive has settled, Belt_SpeedActual is 0, Encoder_Count is constant and every carton position is unchanged across frames; motion resumes only after a new run command actually spins the drive up.","group":"edge","id":"ED-01","needsHmi":false,"objective":"Nothing moves while the drive is stopped; encoder and motion remain consistent at rest.","observeSignals":["Motor_RunCmd","Drive_RunningFB","Belt_SpeedActual","Encoder_Count","PE_Entry","PE_D1Approach"],"requirementRefs":["R-01"],"sourceRefs":["§3 item 4","§8 time evolution","§9 R-01"],"stimulus":"Introduce a carton with the drive never started and observe over several seconds; then start and stop and re-observe after settling.","title":"No motion with drive stopped","worldControls":["carton.introduce"]}],"objective":"Verify the CODESYS PLC application (system under test) against conveyor-slow-belt-spec.md v0.5 on bench map m8-conveyor-1.0.2: start/stop physics consistency, A/B/runout sorting, misroute and blocked-destination handling, WCS handshake behaviour, and fault responses — using only observed PLC evidence, never the simulator's own expectations. Preparation ran no PLC test; no check is claimed passed."},"worldTestTs":"import { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { world } from \"./world.ts\";\nimport type { PlcOutputFrame, RawValue, WorldContext } from \"./contracts.ts\";\n\n// Minimal WorldContext harness recording raw inputs and published entities.\nfunction makeHarness() {\n  const inputs: Record<string, RawValue> = {};\n  const entities = new Map<string, Record<string, unknown>>();\n  const outputs: Record<string, RawValue> = {\n    Motor_RunCmd: false, D1_ExtendCmd: false, D2_ExtendCmd: false,\n    StackLight_Red: false, StackLight_Green: false,\n  };\n  let tickNo = 0;\n  const ctx: WorldContext = {\n    time: { nowMs: 0, deltaMs: 100, tick: 0 },\n    random: { next: () => 0.5, integer: (a: number, _b: number) => a },\n    plc: {\n      readRawOutput: (id: string) => outputs[id] ?? false,\n      writeRawInput: (e) => { inputs[e.signalId] = e.value; },\n      currentOutputFrame: (): PlcOutputFrame => ({ sequence: tickNo, observedAtMs: tickNo * 100, values: { ...outputs } }),\n      currentInputState: () => ({ ...inputs }),\n    },\n    schedule: { at: () => \"sched-1\", cancel: () => undefined },\n    entities: {\n      publish: (s) => { entities.set(s.id, { ...s.state }); },\n      remove: (id: string) => { entities.delete(id); },\n    },\n    evidence: { append: () => undefined },\n    status: { report: () => undefined },\n  };\n  return { ctx, inputs, entities, outputs };\n}\n\ntype Harness = ReturnType<typeof makeHarness>;\n\nasync function tickN(h: Harness, n: number): Promise<void> {\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    await world.tick(h.ctx, { nowMs: (i + 1) * 100, deltaMs: 100, tick: i + 1 });\n  }\n}\n\nasync function setOutputs(h: Harness, patch: Record<string, RawValue>): Promise<void> {\n  Object.assign(h.outputs, patch);\n  await world.onPlcFrame(h.ctx, { sequence: 1, observedAtMs: 0, values: { ...h.outputs } });\n}\n\nasync function freshWorld(h: Harness): Promise<void> {\n  await world.initialize(h.ctx, { seed: 42, worldVersion: \"1.0.2\" });\n}\n\ntest(\"normal state: photoeyes clear, diverts home, drive stopped\", async () => {\n  const h = makeHarness();\n  await freshWorld(h);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.PE_Entry, false);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.D1_HomeFB, true);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.D1_ExtendedFB, false);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.Drive_RunningFB, false);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.Runout_Ready, true);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.Belt_SpeedActual, 0);\n});\n\ntest(\"no motion and no encoder travel while drive is stopped\", async () => {\n  const h = makeHarness();\n  await freshWorld(h);\n  await world.onControl(h.ctx, { id: \"carton.introduce\", payload: { id: \"c1\" }, cause: \"test\" });\n  const enc0 = Number(h.inputs.Encoder_Count ?? 0);\n  await tickN(h, 30);\n  const c = h.entities.get(\"c1\");\n  assert.ok(c, \"carton entity published\");\n  assert.equal(Number(c.positionM), 0, \"carton must not move without drive\");\n  assert.equal(Number(c.velocityMps), 0);\n  assert.equal(Number(h.inputs.Encoder_Count ?? 0), enc0, \"encoder must not advance without belt travel\");\n});\n\ntest(\"motion only under drive, encoder follows travel, deceleration on stop\", async () => {\n  const h = makeHarness();\n  await freshWorld(h);\n  await world.onControl(h.ctx, { id: \"carton.introduce\", payload: { id: \"c2\" }, cause: \"test\" });\n  await setOutputs(h, { Motor_RunCmd: true });\n  await tickN(h, 20);\n  const moving = h.entities.get(\"c2\");\n  assert.ok(moving);\n  const posRun = Number(moving.positionM);\n  const velRun = Number(moving.velocityMps);\n  assert.ok(posRun > 0, \"carton travels under drive\");\n  assert.ok(velRun > 0, \"carton has positive velocity under drive\");\n  const encRun = Number(h.inputs.Encoder_Count);\n  assert.ok(encRun > 0, \"encoder counts from belt travel\");\n  // Encoder travel and carton travel describe the same belt motion (within quantisation).\n  assert.ok(Math.abs(encRun / 1000 - posRun) < 0.05, \"encoder distance consistent with carton travel\");\n  await setOutputs(h, { Motor_RunCmd: false });\n  await tickN(h, 1);\n  const coasting = h.entities.get(\"c2\");\n  assert.ok(coasting);\n  assert.ok(Number(coasting.velocityMps) < velRun, \"velocity decreases after stop command (coast, not instant halt)\");\n  await tickN(h, 30);\n  const stopped = h.entities.get(\"c2\");\n  assert.ok(stopped);\n  assert.equal(Number(stopped.velocityMps), 0, \"carton settles to rest\");\n  const posSettled = Number(stopped.positionM);\n  const encSettled = Number(h.inputs.Encoder_Count);\n  await tickN(h, 10);\n  const later = h.entities.get(\"c2\");\n  assert.ok(later);\n  assert.equal(Number(later.positionM), posSettled, \"position holds after settling\");\n  assert.equal(Number(h.inputs.Encoder_Count), encSettled, \"encoder holds after settling\");\n});\n\ntest(\"photoeyes are derived from carton position\", async () => {\n  const h = makeHarness();\n  await freshWorld(h);\n  await world.onControl(h.ctx, { id: \"carton.introduce\", payload: { id: \"c3\" }, cause: \"test\" });\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.PE_Entry, false);\n  await setOutputs(h, { Motor_RunCmd: true });\n  let sawEntry = false;\n  let sawD1Approach = false;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 60; i++) {\n    await tickN(h, 1);\n    if (h.inputs.PE_Entry === true) sawEntry = true;\n    if (sawEntry && h.inputs.PE_D1Approach === true) sawD1Approach = true;\n  }\n  assert.ok(sawEntry, \"entry photoeye trips as the carton passes it\");\n  assert.ok(sawD1Approach, \"D1 approach trips later, in geometric order\");\n});\n\ntest(\"divert actuator travels with feedback following actual position\", async () => {\n  const h = makeHarness();\n  await freshWorld(h);\n  await setOutputs(h, { D1_ExtendCmd: true });\n  await tickN(h, 1);\n  const midPos = Number(h.inputs.D1_Position);\n  assert.ok(midPos > 0 && midPos < 100, \"divert is mid-travel after one tick\");\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.D1_HomeFB, false, \"neither limit asserted mid-travel\");\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.D1_ExtendedFB, false);\n  await tickN(h, 10);\n  assert.equal(Number(h.inputs.D1_Position), 100);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.D1_ExtendedFB, true);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.D1_HomeFB, false);\n  await setOutputs(h, { D1_ExtendCmd: false });\n  await tickN(h, 10);\n  assert.equal(Number(h.inputs.D1_Position), 0);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.D1_HomeFB, true);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.D1_ExtendedFB, false);\n});\n\ntest(\"extended D1 sends the carton to Exit A only (actual position governs)\", async () => {\n  const h = makeHarness();\n  await freshWorld(h);\n  await world.onControl(h.ctx, { id: \"carton.introduce\", payload: { id: \"c4\" }, cause: \"test\" });\n  await setOutputs(h, { Motor_RunCmd: true, D1_ExtendCmd: true });\n  let sawA = false;\n  let sawRunout = false;\n  let sawB = false;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 120 && h.entities.has(\"c4\"); i++) {\n    await tickN(h, 1);\n    if (h.inputs.PE_ExitA === true) sawA = true;\n    if (h.inputs.PE_Runout === true) sawRunout = true;\n    if (h.inputs.PE_ExitB === true) sawB = true;\n  }\n  assert.ok(sawA, \"diverted carton passes Exit A\");\n  assert.equal(sawRunout, false, \"diverted carton never passes runout\");\n  assert.equal(sawB, false, \"diverted carton never passes Exit B\");\n});\n\ntest(\"home diverts send the carton straight to runout\", async () => {\n  const h = makeHarness();\n  await freshWorld(h);\n  await world.onControl(h.ctx, { id: \"carton.introduce\", payload: { id: \"c5\" }, cause: \"test\" });\n  await setOutputs(h, { Motor_RunCmd: true });\n  let sawRunout = false;\n  let sawA = false;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 160 && h.entities.has(\"c5\"); i++) {\n    await tickN(h, 1);\n    if (h.inputs.PE_Runout === true) sawRunout = true;\n    if (h.inputs.PE_ExitA === true) sawA = true;\n  }\n  assert.ok(sawRunout, \"undiverted carton reaches runout\");\n  assert.equal(sawA, false);\n});\n\ntest(\"drive feedback failure suppresses feedback and motion\", async () => {\n  const h = makeHarness();\n  await freshWorld(h);\n  await world.onControl(h.ctx, { id: \"fault.setDriveFeedbackFailure\", payload: { active: true }, cause: \"test\" });\n  await world.onControl(h.ctx, { id: \"carton.introduce\", payload: { id: \"c6\" }, cause: \"test\" });\n  await setOutputs(h, { Motor_RunCmd: true });\n  await tickN(h, 20);\n  assert.equal(h.inputs.Drive_RunningFB, false);\n  const c = h.entities.get(\"c6\");\n  assert.ok(c);\n  assert.equal(Number(c.positionM), 0, \"no virtual motion when the drive does not run\");\n  await world.onControl(h.ctx, { id: \"fault.clearAll\", cause: \"test\" });\n});\n","worldTs":"import type { GeneratedWorldModule, PlcOutputFrame, RawValue, WorldContext, WorldControl, WorldManifest, WorldSnapshot, WorldTick } from \"./contracts.ts\";\n\n// Slow-belt conveyor — external physical world only.\n// No PLC sequencing, routing, counting, alarm or acceptance logic lives here.\n// Physics: belt drive with accel/decel, cartons carried by the belt, geometric\n// photoeyes, two two-position divert actuators, downstream readiness, faults.\n\nconst BELT_SPEED_MPS = 0.3; // specified, spec section 2 (slow-belt variant)\nconst CARTON_LENGTH_M = 0.3; // suggested starting value, spec section 2\nconst DIVERT_TRAVEL_S = 0.35; // suggested starting value per divert, spec section 2\nconst DRIVE_ACCEL_MPS2 = 0.6; // inferred\nconst DRIVE_DECEL_MPS2 = 0.6; // inferred\nconst ENCODER_COUNTS_PER_M = 1000; // inferred; PLC owns scaling\nconst DRIVE_FB_DELAY_S = 0.1; // inferred\nconst DIVERT_DECISION_PCT = 80; // inferred actual-position threshold at decision point\nconst UINT32_MOD = 4294967296;\n\nconst PE_ENTRY_M = 0.3; // inferred geometry (order specified in section 2)\nconst PE_D1_APPROACH_M = 1.0;\nconst D1_DECISION_M = 1.4;\nconst PE_D2_APPROACH_M = 2.0;\nconst D2_DECISION_M = 2.4;\nconst PE_EXIT_A_M = 2.0; // on A branch, 0.6 m past D1 decision\nconst PE_EXIT_B_M = 3.0; // on B branch, 0.6 m past D2 decision\nconst PE_RUNOUT_M = 3.2; // main lane\nconst REMOVE_PAST_SENSOR_M = 0.5;\n\ntype Branch = \"main\" | \"A\" | \"B\";\n\ninterface CartonState {\n  id: string;\n  positionM: number;\n  velocityMps: number;\n  lengthM: number;\n  branch: Branch;\n  passedD1: boolean;\n  passedD2: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface FaultState {\n  driveFeedbackFailure: boolean;\n  overload: boolean;\n  divertJamD1: boolean;\n  divertJamD2: boolean;\n  contradictoryD1: boolean;\n  contradictoryD2: boolean;\n  cartonJam: boolean;\n  stuckSignals: Record<string, boolean>;\n  bounceSignals: string[];\n}\n\ninterface WorldState {\n  timeMs: number;\n  tickCount: number;\n  beltSpeedMps: number;\n  totalTravelM: number;\n  driveFbTimerS: number;\n  d1PositionPct: number;\n  d2PositionPct: number;\n  cartons: CartonState[];\n  nextCartonSeq: number;\n  downstreamReady: { A: boolean; B: boolean; Runout: boolean };\n  faults: FaultState;\n  plcOutputs: Record<string, RawValue>;\n}\n\nfunction defaultFaults(): FaultState {\n  return {\n    driveFeedbackFailure: false,\n    overload: false,\n    divertJamD1: false,\n    divertJamD2: false,\n    contradictoryD1: false,\n    contradictoryD2: false,\n    cartonJam: false,\n    stuckSignals: {},\n    bounceSignals: [],\n  };\n}\n\nfunction defaultState(): WorldState {\n  return {\n    timeMs: 0,\n    tickCount: 0,\n    beltSpeedMps: 0,\n    totalTravelM: 0,\n    driveFbTimerS: 0,\n    d1PositionPct: 0,\n    d2PositionPct: 0,\n    cartons: [],\n    nextCartonSeq: 1,\n    downstreamReady: { A: true, B: true, Runout: true },\n    faults: defaultFaults(),\n    plcOutputs: {\n      Motor_RunCmd: false,\n      D1_ExtendCmd: false,\n      D2_ExtendCmd: false,\n      StackLight_Red: false,\n      StackLight_Green: false,\n    },\n  };\n}\n\nlet state: WorldState = defaultState();\n\nfunction outBool(id: string): boolean {\n  return state.plcOutputs[id] === true;\n}\n\nfunction payloadBool(payload: Record<string, unknown> | undefined, key: string, fallback: boolean): boolean {\n  if (payload && typeof payload[key] === \"boolean\") return payload[key] as boolean;\n  return fallback;\n}\n\nfunction payloadText(payload: Record<string, unknown> | undefined, keys: string[]): string {\n  if (!payload) return \"\";\n  for (const k of keys) {\n    const v = payload[k];\n    if (typeof v === \"string\") return v;\n    if (typeof v === \"number\") return String(v);\n  }\n  return \"\";\n}\n\nfunction divertSelector(text: string): \"D1\" | \"D2\" | \"both\" {\n  const t = text.toLowerCase();\n  if (t.includes(\"d2\") || t === \"2\" || t.includes(\"second\")) return \"D2\";\n  if (t.includes(\"d1\") || t === \"1\" || t.includes(\"first\")) return \"D1\";\n  return \"both\";\n}\n\nconst KNOWN_BOOL_INPUTS: string[] = [\n  \"PE_Entry\", \"PE_D1Approach\", \"PE_D2Approach\", \"PE_ExitA\", \"PE_ExitB\", \"PE_Runout\",\n  \"D1_HomeFB\", \"D1_ExtendedFB\", \"D2_HomeFB\", \"D2_ExtendedFB\",\n  \"Drive_RunningFB\", \"Drive_Overload\", \"ExitA_Ready\", \"ExitB_Ready\", \"Runout_Ready\",\n];\n\nfunction normaliseSignalId(text: string): string {\n  if (KNOWN_BOOL_INPUTS.includes(text)) return text;\n  const t = text.toLowerCase();\n  if (t.includes(\"d1\") && t.includes(\"approach\")) return \"PE_D1Approach\";\n  if (t.includes(\"d2\") && t.includes(\"approach\")) return \"PE_D2Approach\";\n  if (t.includes(\"entry\")) return \"PE_Entry\";\n  if (t.includes(\"exita\") || t.endsWith(\"a\")) return \"PE_ExitA\";\n  if (t.includes(\"exitb\") || t.endsWith(\"b\")) return \"PE_ExitB\";\n  if (t.includes(\"runout\")) return \"PE_Runout\";\n  if (t.includes(\"d1\") && t.includes(\"extended\")) return \"D1_ExtendedFB\";\n  if (t.includes(\"d1\") && t.includes(\"home\")) return \"D1_HomeFB\";\n  if (t.includes(\"d2\") && t.includes(\"extended\")) return \"D2_ExtendedFB\";\n  if (t.includes(\"d2\") && t.includes(\"home\")) return \"D2_HomeFB\";\n  if (t.includes(\"running\")) return \"Drive_RunningFB\";\n  if (t.includes(\"overload\")) return \"Drive_Overload\";\n  return text;\n}\n\nfunction sensorBlocked(carton: CartonState, sensorM: number): boolean {\n  // positionM is the leading edge; the carton body spans [pos-length, pos].\n  return carton.positionM >= sensorM && carton.positionM - carton.lengthM <= sensorM;\n}\n\nfunction anyCartonAt(sensorM: number, branch: Branch | \"any\"): boolean {\n  return state.cartons.some((c) => (branch === \"any\" || c.branch === branch) && sensorBlocked(c, sensorM));\n}\n\nfunction encoderCount(): number {\n  const raw = Math.floor(state.totalTravelM * ENCODER_COUNTS_PER_M);\n  return ((raw % UINT32_MOD) + UINT32_MOD) % UINT32_MOD;\n}\n\nfunction writeAllInputs(ctx: WorldContext, causePrefix: string): void {\n  const f = state.faults;\n  const physical: Record<string, RawValue> = {};\n  physical[\"PE_Entry\"] = anyCartonAt(PE_ENTRY_M, \"any\");\n  physical[\"PE_D1Approach\"] = anyCartonAt(PE_D1_APPROACH_M, \"any\");\n  physical[\"PE_D2Approach\"] = anyCartonAt(PE_D2_APPROACH_M, \"main\");\n  physical[\"PE_ExitA\"] = anyCartonAt(PE_EXIT_A_M, \"A\");\n  physical[\"PE_ExitB\"] = anyCartonAt(PE_EXIT_B_M, \"B\");\n  physical[\"PE_Runout\"] = anyCartonAt(PE_RUNOUT_M, \"main\");\n  physical[\"D1_HomeFB\"] = state.d1PositionPct <= 0;\n  physical[\"D1_ExtendedFB\"] = state.d1PositionPct >= 100;\n  physical[\"D2_HomeFB\"] = state.d2PositionPct <= 0;\n  physical[\"D2_ExtendedFB\"] = state.d2PositionPct >= 100;\n  const driveEnergised = outBool(\"Motor_RunCmd\") && !f.overload && !f.driveFeedbackFailure;\n  physical[\"Drive_RunningFB\"] = !f.driveFeedbackFailure && driveEnergised && state.driveFbTimerS >= DRIVE_FB_DELAY_S;\n  physical[\"Drive_Overload\"] = f.overload;\n  physical[\"ExitA_Ready\"] = state.downstreamReady.A;\n  physical[\"ExitB_Ready\"] = state.downstreamReady.B;\n  physical[\"Runout_Ready\"] = state.downstreamReady.Runout;\n  if (f.contradictoryD1) { physical[\"D1_HomeFB\"] = true; physical[\"D1_ExtendedFB\"] = true; }\n  if (f.contradictoryD2) { physical[\"D2_HomeFB\"] = true; physical[\"D2_ExtendedFB\"] = true; }\n\n  for (const id of KNOWN_BOOL_INPUTS) {\n    let value = physical[id] === true;\n    let cause = causePrefix + \":physical-state\";\n    if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(f.stuckSignals, id)) {\n      value = f.stuckSignals[id] === true;\n      cause = causePrefix + \":fault-sensor-stuck:\" + id;\n    } else if (f.bounceSignals.includes(id)) {\n      value = state.tickCount % 2 === 0 ? value : !value;\n      cause = causePrefix + \":fault-sensor-bounce:\" + id;\n    }\n    ctx.plc.writeRawInput({ signalId: id, value, cause });\n  }\n  ctx.plc.writeRawInput({ signalId: \"Belt_SpeedActual\", value: state.beltSpeedMps, cause: causePrefix + \":belt-dynamics\" });\n  const current = f.overload ? 8 : (BELT_SPEED_MPS > 0 ? 2 * (state.beltSpeedMps / BELT_SPEED_MPS) : 0);\n  ctx.plc.writeRawInput({ signalId: \"Drive_Current\", value: current, cause: causePrefix + \":drive-load-model\" });\n  ctx.plc.writeRawInput({ signalId: \"D1_Position\", value: state.d1PositionPct, cause: causePrefix + \":divert1-actuator-position\" });\n  ctx.plc.writeRawInput({ signalId: \"D2_Position\", value: state.d2PositionPct, cause: causePrefix + \":divert2-actuator-position\" });\n  ctx.plc.writeRawInput({ signalId: \"Encoder_Count\", value: encoderCount(), cause: causePrefix + \":encoder-from-belt-travel\" });\n}\n\nfunction publishCartons(ctx: WorldContext): void {\n  for (const c of state.cartons) {\n    ctx.entities.publish({\n      id: c.id,\n      type: \"carton\",\n      state: {\n        positionM: c.positionM,\n        velocityMps: c.velocityMps,\n        lengthM: c.lengthM,\n        branch: c.branch,\n        passedD1: c.passedD1,\n        passedD2: c.passedD2,\n      },\n    });\n  }\n}\n\nfunction stepActuator(currentPct: number, extendCmd: boolean, jammed: boolean, dtS: number): number {\n  if (jammed) return currentPct;\n  const rate = 100 / DIVERT_TRAVEL_S;\n  if (extendCmd) return Math.min(100, currentPct + rate * dtS);\n  return Math.max(0, currentPct - rate * dtS);\n}\n\nfunction removalLimitM(c: CartonState): number {\n  if (c.branch === \"A\") return PE_EXIT_A_M + REMOVE_PAST_SENSOR_M;\n  if (c.branch === \"B\") return PE_EXIT_B_M + REMOVE_PAST_SENSOR_M;\n  return PE_RUNOUT_M + REMOVE_PAST_SENSOR_M;\n}\n\nconst manifest: WorldManifest = {\n  packageVersion: \"1.0.2\",\n  stateSchemaVersion: \"1.0.0\",\n  worldId: \"m8-conveyor-1.0.2\",\n  name: \"Slow-belt conveyor variant (M8)\",\n  tickMs: 100,\n  signals: [\n    { id: \"PE_Entry\", name: \"PE_Entry\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"conveyor\", role: \"sensor.entry\", description: \"Carton blocks the entry beam; derived from carton position and length.\" },\n    { id: \"PE_D1Approach\", name: \"PE_D1Approach\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"conveyor\", role: \"sensor.d1Approach\", description: \"Carton in the decision window before divert 1.\" },\n    { id: \"PE_D2Approach\", name: \"PE_D2Approach\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"conveyor\", role: \"sensor.d2Approach\", description: \"Carton on the main lane toward divert 2.\" },\n    { id: \"PE_ExitA\", name: \"PE_ExitA\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"conveyor\", role: \"sensor.exitA\", description: \"Carton passes diverted exit A.\" },\n    { id: \"PE_ExitB\", name: \"PE_ExitB\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"conveyor\", role: \"sensor.exitB\", description: \"Carton passes diverted exit B.\" },\n    { id: \"PE_Runout\", name: \"PE_Runout\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"conveyor\", role: \"sensor.runout\", description: \"Carton passes the straight runout.\" },\n    { id: \"D1_HomeFB\", name: \"D1_HomeFB\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: true, deviceId: \"divert1\", role: \"divert1.homeFeedback\", description: \"Divert 1 fully home; false during travel or failure.\" },\n    { id: \"D1_ExtendedFB\", name: \"D1_ExtendedFB\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"divert1\", role: \"divert1.extendedFeedback\", description: \"Divert 1 fully extended.\" },\n    { id: \"D2_HomeFB\", name: \"D2_HomeFB\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: true, deviceId: \"divert2\", role: \"divert2.homeFeedback\", description: \"Divert 2 fully home.\" },\n    { id: \"D2_ExtendedFB\", name: \"D2_ExtendedFB\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"divert2\", role: \"divert2.extendedFeedback\", description: \"Divert 2 fully extended.\" },\n    { id: \"Drive_RunningFB\", name: \"Drive_RunningFB\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"drive\", role: \"drive.runningFeedback\", description: \"Actual drive-running feedback, delayed after Motor_RunCmd and suppressible on failure.\" },\n    { id: \"Drive_Overload\", name: \"Drive_Overload\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"drive\", role: \"drive.overload\", description: \"Simulated overload/trip input; normally false.\" },\n    { id: \"ExitA_Ready\", name: \"ExitA_Ready\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: true, deviceId: \"downstream\", role: \"downstream.exitAReady\", description: \"Destination A can accept a carton.\" },\n    { id: \"ExitB_Ready\", name: \"ExitB_Ready\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: true, deviceId: \"downstream\", role: \"downstream.exitBReady\", description: \"Destination B can accept a carton.\" },\n    { id: \"Runout_Ready\", name: \"Runout_Ready\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: true, deviceId: \"downstream\", role: \"downstream.runoutReady\", description: \"Runout can accept a carton; normally true.\" },\n    { id: \"Belt_SpeedActual\", name: \"Belt_SpeedActual\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"REAL\", normalValue: 0, deviceId: \"drive\", role: \"drive.speedActual\", description: \"Actual belt speed in m/s.\" },\n    { id: \"Drive_Current\", name: \"Drive_Current\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"REAL\", normalValue: 0, deviceId: \"drive\", role: \"drive.current\", description: \"Simulated drive current in A (diagnostic).\" },\n    { id: \"D1_Position\", name: \"D1_Position\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"REAL\", normalValue: 0, deviceId: \"divert1\", role: \"divert1.position\", description: \"Divert 1 actual position, 0-100 percent.\" },\n    { id: \"D2_Position\", name: \"D2_Position\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"REAL\", normalValue: 0, deviceId: \"divert2\", role: \"divert2.position\", description: \"Divert 2 actual position, 0-100 percent.\" },\n    { id: \"Encoder_Count\", name: \"Encoder_Count\", direction: \"world_to_plc\", dataType: \"UDINT\", normalValue: 0, deviceId: \"drive\", role: \"motion.encoderCount\", description: \"Encoder counts from belt travel, quantised, UDINT wrap; PLC owns scaling.\" },\n    { id: \"Motor_RunCmd\", name: \"Motor_RunCmd\", direction: \"plc_to_world\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"drive\", role: \"drive.runCommand\", description: \"PLC command to the belt drive. Cartons move only if the simulated drive actually runs.\" },\n    { id: \"D1_ExtendCmd\", name: \"D1_ExtendCmd\", direction: \"plc_to_world\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"divert1\", role: \"divert1.extendCommand\", description: \"Extend divert 1 to exit A; deassert returns home.\" },\n    { id: \"D2_ExtendCmd\", name: \"D2_ExtendCmd\", direction: \"plc_to_world\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"divert2\", role: \"divert2.extendCommand\", description: \"Extend divert 2 to exit B; deassert returns home.\" },\n    { id: \"StackLight_Red\", name: \"StackLight_Red\", direction: \"plc_to_world\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"stacklight\", role: \"indication.stackRed\", description: \"Optional visible machine-fault indication.\" },\n    { id: \"StackLight_Green\", name: \"StackLight_Green\", direction: \"plc_to_world\", dataType: \"BOOL\", normalValue: false, deviceId: \"stacklight\", role: \"indication.stackGreen\", description: \"Optional visible running/ready indication.\" },\n  ],\n  controls: [\n    { id: \"carton.introduce\", description: \"Introduce a physical carton at the entry (position 0). Payload may carry id/itemId; route is ignored by the